<article class="env-lemma" id="0CIZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CIZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0CIZ">101.36.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ be morphisms of algebraic stacks. If $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is unramified and $\mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is DM, then $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ is unramified. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is unramified. By Lemma <a href="/tag/050M" data-tag="050M">101.4.12</a> the morphism $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ is DM. Choose a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[d] \ar[r] &  V \ar[d] \ar[r] &  W \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{X} \ar[r] &  \mathcal{Y} \ar[r] &  \mathcal{Z} }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with $U, V, W$ algebraic spaces, with $W \to \mathcal{Z}$ surjective smooth, $V \to \mathcal{Y} \times _\mathcal {Z} W$ surjective étale, and $U \to \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Y} V$ surjective étale (see Lemma <a href="/tag/0CIA" data-tag="0CIA">101.21.7</a>). Then also $U \to \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Z} W$ is surjective and étale. Hence we know that $U \to W$ is unramified and we have to show that $U \to V$ is unramified. This follows from Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/06G6" data-tag="06G6">67.38.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>